1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,891
The night before Karwa Chauth,
Aman said: "This time…

2
00:00:04,891 --> 00:00:06,814
I'm fasting too."

3
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:10,834
A husband fasting? Bua
ji dropped her spoon…

4
00:00:10,834 --> 00:00:12,653
but she didn't know one thing.

5
00:00:12,653 --> 00:00:16,924
"Have you lost it? A man, fasting?
What will people say!"

6
00:00:16,924 --> 00:00:19,914
Neha looked down… Aman went quiet.

7
00:00:20,414 --> 00:00:23,164
The answer is 3,000 years old…

8
00:00:23,164 --> 00:00:25,517
in the Rigveda: Surya's wedding.

9
00:00:25,917 --> 00:00:30,583
Before the fire, the groom took
her hand… and HE made the first
vow.

10
00:00:30,953 --> 00:00:35,844
"I take your hand for good
fortune, so that with me, your
husband,

11
00:00:35,844 --> 00:00:37,825
you live to old age."

12
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:44,774
"I take your hand… so that you
grow old with me."

13
00:00:44,774 --> 00:00:48,793
Jaradashti = old age, together.

14
00:00:48,793 --> 00:00:52,496
The wish for a long life together
was two-way from day one.

15
00:00:53,006 --> 00:00:57,425
Next evening, the moon rose… and
they broke the fast together.

16
00:00:57,565 --> 00:00:58,565
Tomorrow…

17
00:00:58,565 --> 00:01:00,057
YOU set her thali.

18
00:01:00,057 --> 00:01:01,937
A vow isn't one person's…

19
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:03,446
it's both.

20
00:01:04,116 --> 00:01:08,275
Should husbands fast
too? Yes or no? Comment.

21
00:01:08,345 --> 00:01:12,511
Send this to the friend who says,
"That's the wife's job."
